{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "a1b2c3d4-e5f6-7890-abcd-ef1234567890",
    "name": "Scoriet CLI API v1",
    "description": "Public API for Scoriet (Schema-to-Stack Studio). All endpoints live under /cli/v1/*.\n\n## Rate limits (per Passport token)\n\n- **cli-default**: 1000 requests/hour — applies to every authenticated endpoint. Generous enough that legitimate clients (CLI, svc polling, Postman) never hit it.\n- **cli-generate**: 30 requests/hour — additionally applied to `POST /generate/`. Each generation costs credits and queue-worker time, so this is the real DoS/credit-drain guard. Progress/download/cancel are NOT counted against this limit (polling stays unrestricted up to cli-default).\n- **Unauthenticated** calls fall back to per-IP buckets (60/h or 5/h respectively).\n\nWhen exhausted, you get HTTP 429 with a `Retry-After` header — Postman/curl/CLI will show the seconds until your bucket refills.\n\n## Response envelope\n\n**Every** response on this surface follows the same shape:\n\n**Success (2xx):**\n```json\n{\n  \"success\": true,\n  \"data\":    { ... },                  // the actual payload\n  \"meta\":    { \"updated_fields\": [...], \"pagination\": {...} },  // optional\n  \"warnings\": [ { \"code\": \"...\", \"message\": \"...\" } ]            // optional\n}\n```\n\n**Error (4xx/5xx):**\n```json\n{\n  \"success\": false,\n  \"error\": {\n    \"code\":    \"VALIDATION_FAILED\",     // machine-readable\n    \"message\": \"Human-readable\",\n    \"details\": { \"name\": [\"already taken\"] }  // optional\n  }\n}\n```\n\nCommon error codes: `VALIDATION_FAILED`, `NOT_FOUND`, `UNAUTHORIZED`, `FORBIDDEN`, `CONFLICT`, `INSUFFICIENT_CREDITS`, `RATE_LIMITED`, `SERVER_ERROR`.\n\nLegacy keys (`template`, `templates`, `schemas`, `settings`, etc.) are still inside `data` — e.g. `data.template`, `data.templates`. The middleware moves them there automatically so the wire-shape is stable.\n\n## Quick Start\n\n1. Open the collection variables (top-level **Variables** tab) and fill in `email` + `password`.\n2. Run **🔑 Auth → Login (authorize)** — the response auto-saves the bearer token into `cli_token` via the test script (it knows to unwrap `data.token.access_token`).\n3. Every other request reuses `{{cli_token}}` automatically.\n\n## Variables\n\n- `base_url` – defaults to `http://10.0.0.8:8000/cli/v1` (change to your install)\n- `email`, `password` – your Scoriet account\n- `cli_token` – auto-set after login\n- `template_id`, `project_id`, `schema_id`, `job_id` – pre-filled with sample ids; replace with your own after listing\n\n## Auth\n\n- Public endpoints (`/system/*`, `/auth/authorize`, `/auth/verify-2fa`) skip auth\n- Everything else inherits Bearer-token auth from the collection level",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{cli_token}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
