    {
      "name": "📄 Template Files",
      "description": "Full CRUD on template files. `list` returns metadata only (cheap); `show` returns one file WITH its `file_content` bytes; `update` is a partial PUT that supports content edits.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "List files in template",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Accept", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/templates/{{template_id}}/files",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["templates", "{{template_id}}", "files"]
            },
            "description": "Returns metadata for every file in the template — `file_name`, `file_path`, `content_size`, `file_order`, etc. **`file_content` is NOT included** to keep list responses small even when a template has many large files. Use **Get single file** to fetch the bytes."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Get single file (with content)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Accept", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/templates/{{template_id}}/files/{{file_id}}",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["templates", "{{template_id}}", "files", "{{file_id}}"]
            },
            "description": "Returns the file metadata **plus** the full `file_content` (the actual template bytes). Same access rules as the list endpoint — owners, public templates, and system templates are readable."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Add file to template",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
              { "key": "Accept", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"file_name\": \"example.php\",\n  \"file_path\": \"src/\",\n  \"output_path\": \"src/\",\n  \"file_content\": \"<?php\\n\\n// Generated by {:projectname:}\\n\\nclass Example {}\\n\",\n  \"file_type\": \"template\",\n  \"content_type\": \"text\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/templates/{{template_id}}/files",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["templates", "{{template_id}}", "files"]
            },
            "description": "**Required:** `file_name`, `file_content`.\n\n**Optional:** `file_path`, `output_path`, `file_type`, `content_type`.\n\nUse `\\n` for newlines in JSON. `file_content` may contain Scoriet template syntax like `{:projectname:}`, `{:for nmaxtables:}`, etc."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Update file (partial)",
          "request": {
            "method": "PUT",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
              { "key": "Accept", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"file_content\": \"<?php\\n\\n// Updated content for {:projectname:}\\nclass Example {}\\n\",\n  \"file_order\": 2\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/templates/{{template_id}}/files/{{file_id}}",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["templates", "{{template_id}}", "files", "{{file_id}}"]
            },
            "description": "**Partial update** — only fields you send change.\n\n**Editable fields:** `file_name`, `file_path`, `output_path`, `file_content`, `file_type`, `content_type`, `file_order`.\n\n**Rules:**\n- Only the template creator can update files.\n- System templates are read-only via CLI.\n- Renaming to an existing file_name within the same template returns 409.\n- A body with only unknown fields returns 422 + `expected_fields` list.\n- Mix of known + unknown fields: update succeeds, `warnings.unknown_fields` lists the ignored ones.\n\nResponse includes `updated_fields` echoing what actually persisted."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Delete file from template (HARD)",
          "request": {
            "method": "DELETE",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Accept", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/templates/{{template_id}}/files/{{file_id}}",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["templates", "{{template_id}}", "files", "{{file_id}}"]
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "🗄️ Database / Schemas",
      "description": "Schema CRUD + SQL import/export. The SQL import is how external tools push table structures into Scoriet.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "List schemas",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Accept", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/database/list?project_id={{project_id}}",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["database", "list"],
              "query": [
                { "key": "project_id", "value": "{{project_id}}", "description": "Optional — filter to one project. Omit (or disable) to list every schema you have access to (own + public).", "disabled": true }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Lists database schemas.\n\n**Without `project_id`** (default): every schema you can access — your own private ones plus all public schemas.\n\n**With `project_id`**: only the schemas linked to that project. Toggle the query parameter on (uncheck `Disabled`) to filter."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Create empty schema",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
              { "key": "Accept", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"schema_name\": \"postman_test_schema\",\n  \"description\": \"Created from Postman\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/database/create",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["database", "create"]
            },
            "description": "Creates a new (empty) schema owned by the current user.\n\n**Body fields:**\n- `schema_name` — required, must be unique per user.\n- `description` — optional.\n- `visibility` — optional, `private` (default) or `public`.\n- `project_id` — optional, when present the schema is auto-linked to that project. Omit to create a standalone schema you can link to one or more projects later via `/projects/{id}/schemas` (or any equivalent association endpoint)."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Get schema structure",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Accept", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/database/{{schema_id}}/structure",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["database", "{{schema_id}}", "structure"]
            },
            "description": "Returns tables, fields, constraints — the full JSON description of the schema's latest version."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "List schema versions",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Accept", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/database/{{schema_id}}/versions",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["database", "{{schema_id}}", "versions"]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Import SQL into schema",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
              { "key": "Accept", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"schema_id\": {{schema_id}},\n  \"sql_content\": \"CREATE TABLE products (\\n  id BIGINT UNSIGNED AUTO_INCREMENT PRIMARY KEY,\\n  name VARCHAR(255) NOT NULL,\\n  price DECIMAL(10,2) DEFAULT 0,\\n  created_at TIMESTAMP DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP\\n);\",\n  \"description\": \"Initial product table\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/database/import-sql",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["database", "import-sql"]
            },
            "description": "Parses raw SQL DDL (CREATE TABLE / ALTER TABLE / etc.) and persists it as schema tables/fields/constraints.\n\n**Optional:** `schema_version` — if set, imports into that specific version. Otherwise creates a new version."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Copy version (snapshot to new version)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
              { "key": "Accept", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"schema_id\": {{schema_id}},\n  \"source_version\": 1,\n  \"description\": \"Branched from v1\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/database/copy-version",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["database", "copy-version"]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Export schema as SQL",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
              { "key": "Accept", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"schema_id\": {{schema_id}},\n  \"format\": \"mysql\",\n  \"version\": 1\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/database/export",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["database", "export"]
            },
            "description": "**Format:** `mysql` | `postgresql`.\n\nReturns the schema as DDL ready for execution."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Delete schema (HARD)",
          "request": {
            "method": "DELETE",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Accept", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/database/{{schema_id}}",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["database", "{{schema_id}}"]
            },
            "description": "⚠️ Removes the schema, all versions, all tables, all fields. Permanent."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Delete schema version (HARD)",
          "request": {
            "method": "DELETE",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Accept", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/database/{{schema_id}}/versions/{{schema_version_id}}",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["database", "{{schema_id}}", "versions", "{{schema_version_id}}"]
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "⚡ Generate",
      "description": "Trigger code generation, poll progress, download ZIP.\n\n**Async flow** (backend dispatches a queue job):\n\n1. **Trigger code generation** → returns 202 with `job_id` and `status: pending`. Auto-saved to `{{job_id}}`.\n2. **Get generation progress** → poll every 1–2 seconds. Status transitions: `pending` → `running` → `completed` | `failed` | `cancelled`. Includes `progress_pct` and timing fields.\n3. **Download generated ZIP** → only valid after `status: completed`. Returns 425 (Too Early) while still pending/running, 410 (Gone) for cancelled/failed jobs.\n4. **Cancel generation job** (optional) → flips a cancel flag; the worker honours it at its next checkpoint (start of job + after generation returns). Returns 409 if the job is already in a terminal state.\n\nThe queue worker (`php artisan queue:work`) must be running for jobs to actually execute. In dev, `composer run dev` includes it.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Trigger code generation",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "const data = json && json.data ? json.data : {};",
                  "if (data.job_id) {",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set('job_id', data.job_id);",
                  "    console.log('🎬 Job started, id saved: ' + data.job_id);",
                  "}"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
              { "key": "Accept", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"project_id\": {{project_id}},\n  \"template_id\": {{template_id}},\n  \"output_format\": \"zip\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/generate/",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["generate", ""]
            },
            "description": "Dispatches a background queue job and returns **immediately** (HTTP 202).\n\n**Response:** `{success: true, data: {job_id, status: 'pending', progress_url, download_url, cancel_url}}` — `job_id` is auto-saved to {{job_id}}.\n\nThen poll **Get generation progress** until `status` is `completed`."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Get generation progress",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Accept", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/generate/progress/{{job_id}}",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["generate", "progress", "{{job_id}}"]
            },
            "description": "Poll every 1–2 seconds. Returns the live job state:\n\n```\n{\n  status: 'pending' | 'running' | 'completed' | 'failed' | 'cancelled',\n  progress_pct: 0..100,\n  created_at, started_at, completed_at, failed_at,\n  // when completed:\n  files_count, gtree_nodes, download_url,\n  // when failed:\n  errors: [ ... ]\n}\n```\n\nNo blocking — each call returns whatever the worker has written to the state file at that moment."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Download generated ZIP",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Accept", "value": "application/octet-stream" }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/generate/download/{{job_id}}",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["generate", "download", "{{job_id}}"]
            },
            "description": "Returns a ZIP stream. In Postman click **Save Response → Save to a file**.\n\n**Status gates:**\n- `425 Too Early` if status is `pending` or `running` — keep polling.\n- `410 Gone` if status is `cancelled` or `failed` — job will never produce a file.\n- `200 OK` only when status is `completed`."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Cancel generation job",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Accept", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/generate/cancel/{{job_id}}",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["generate", "cancel", "{{job_id}}"]
            },
            "description": "**Co-operative cancel** — sets a flag in the state file. The worker checks it at its yield points (start of handle() and after the generate call returns), so a job already mid-generate-call will finish that call before honouring the cancel.\n\nReturns `409 Conflict` if the job is already in a terminal state (completed/failed/cancelled)."
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
